ically, or get back to the user unless a real automation or reminder has been created through an available tool and confirmed.\",\n      \"directive\": \"This condition holds. Do not promise background monitoring or that you will remove the event later without the user's confirmation and an explicitly created automation/reminder. Offer to perform the cancellation immediately after the user confirms the required details, or offer instructions the user can follow if they prefer to do it themselves.\",\n      \"finding\": \"User asked a one-off action: \\\"take it off the calendar\\\" (no automation or reminder already created).\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"condition\": \"Treat user files, emails, calendars, images, contacts, locations, and private documents as private. Minimize disclosure. Do not infer sensitive attributes from ambiguous data. Do not identify unknown people.\",\n      \"directive\": \"This condition holds. Minimize disclosure of private calendar details: ask only for the minimal confirmations needed (event title/date/time, scope, and notification preference). Avoid listing or exposing attendee email addresses or other private metadata unless strictly required and explicitly authorized by the user.\",\n      \"finding\": \"User request targets a calendar event (calendar content is private).\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"condition\": \"Policy precedence and operating model rule 1: apply this section conservatively when the user request, tool choice, artifact manifest, operation, domain hint, or risk hint indicates that the rule is relevant. Preserve dependencies and definitions. If the rule protects safety, privacy, tool integrity, current information, destructive actions, or numeric accuracy, retain it unless it is confidently excludable.\",\n      \"directive\": \"This condition holds. Apply the policy conservatively: retain privacy, destructive-action, and tool-integrity obligations for this calendar cancellation and do not drop them because the user phrase